meta {
  name: Create a hosted connect link
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/connect-sessions
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "externalUserId": "x",
    "platforms": [
      "twitter"
    ]
  }
}

tests {
  test('status is successful', function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([201]);
  });
}

docs {
  Mints a single-use link, open for one hour, that lets one of your end users connect a social account into your workspace with no FoPost login, on a page carrying your `branding`. The account is tagged with `externalUserId`. `redirectUrl` must be on a domain in the workspace redirect allowlist (dashboard → API Keys); the user is sent there with `status`, `platform`, `account_id` and `external_user_id` once connected. `workspaceId` may be omitted for a key bound to one workspace.

  Requires the `accounts` scope when using an API key.

  Requires an active subscription; without one the request fails with 403 `subscription_required`.

  **Scope:** `accounts`

  **Optional fields** (not in the example body):
  - `workspaceId`: string (uuid)
  - `redirectUrl`: string (uri)
  - `branding`: object
}
